@startuml
concise "DAT line" as DAT
concise "Read Wait" as RW
concise "Stop At Block Gap Request (Control)" as SABGR
concise "Continue Request (Control)" as CR
concise "DAT Line Active (Status)" as DLA
concise "Read Transfer Active (Status)" as RTA
concise "Block Gap Event (Interrupt)" as BGE
concise "Transfer Complete (Interrupt)" as TC

@0
DAT is idle
RW is low
SABGR is low
CR is low
DLA is low
RTA is low
BGE is low
TC is low

@10
DAT is "Last block"
RW is high

@20
SABGR is high

@30
CR is high
SABGR is low

@40
DLA is high
RW is low

@50
RTA is high

@100
DLA is low
RTA is low

@110
TC is high

@120
TC is low

@enduml